@startuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

participant "Customer" as Customer
participant "Website / Mobile App" as Channel
participant "Booking Controller" as Controller
participant "Booking Service" as Service
database "Redis Cache" as Redis
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Calendar Service" as Calendar
participant "Microsoft Graph API" as GraphAPI
participant "Exchange Online" as Exchange
queue "RabbitMQ" as MQ
participant "Notification Service" as Notifier

Customer -> Channel: Click free slot
Channel -> Controller: POST /api/bookings
Controller -> Service: createBooking(request)

Service -> Redis: tryReserve(advisorId, startTime)
Redis --> Service: OK (reserved with TTL 5 min)

Service -> DB: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE (pessimistic lock)
DB --> Service: Slot row (locked)

Service -> Calendar: isSlotAvailable(advisorId, startTime, endTime)
Calendar -> GraphAPI: GET /users/{id}/calendar/calendarView
GraphAPI -> Exchange: Check calendar
Exchange --> GraphAPI: Free
GraphAPI --> Calendar: Available
Calendar --> Service: true

Service -> Calendar: createEvent(...)
Calendar -> GraphAPI: POST /users/{id}/events
GraphAPI -> Exchange: Create appointment
Exchange --> GraphAPI: Event created
GraphAPI --> Calendar: event-id-123
Calendar --> Service: event-id-123

Service -> DB: save(booking)
Service -> DB: slot.setBooked(true)

Service -> MQ: publish "booking.confirmed"
Service --> Controller: BookingResponse (CONFIRMED)
Controller --> Channel: 200 OK
Channel --> Customer: "Booking confirmed!"

MQ -> Notifier: Consume "booking.confirmed"
Notifier -> GraphAPI: POST /users/{sender}/sendMail
GraphAPI -> Exchange: Send email
note right of Notifier: Retry 5 times with backoff\nif email fails (Dead Letter Queue)

@enduml
